laurel 3031: the USB panic hold serves in every case the stopped USB thread can leave: the event ring is read against a mark of where ud_service_events was, the data path (the one RX TRB) is re-armed from a known state at the hold start and after 15 s with no frame, a completion for a TRB the controller still owns is not a frame, a nested panic inside the hold resets in 5 s instead of a silent spin, and the bark line of the hold uses kdb_printf (kprintf spins on a lock a stopped CPU can hold). Cause of 2026-11-03 17:56:16 (holding, then no pong for 44 min) [I]: the panic IPI stopped ud_thread between the frame read and ud_rx_arm, or between the ack and the handling of the RX completion: no TRB, no receive, while the TX side still sent "holding". Both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/watchdog.md section 15.

